EDIT TASK (district migration wave 2): the included file tasks_out/worker_lighthouse.js is the current lighthouse module; its ANCHOR is { gx: 4.5, gy: 7.5 }, too close to the hearth. The island is 48x48 tiles and must USE its space. Move the lighthouse to the PONDSIDE district (southeast fishing corner) per the town plan: read the anchor from window.GuildZones.PONDSIDE when available, falling back to the literal { gx: 14, gy: 15 }. That looks like: const Z = (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.GuildZones && window.GuildZones.PONDSIDE) || { gx: 14, gy: 15 }; const ANCHOR = { gx: Z.gx, gy: Z.gy };
Rules: keep EVERY behavior identical (beam sweep, boost, glow, update/draw/__probe contract, window.GuildLighthouse global); change ONLY the anchor position and any header comment that names the old spot; add a header comment line naming the district: PONDSIDE district (LAYOUT.md). Keep the proven module conventions: self-installing ES module, no imports, no top-level DOM access, typeof guards.
OUTPUT: the complete updated file, wrapped in one standard fenced code block (three backticks, NO language tag). Never place literal triple-backtick characters inside the code. One line of prose max outside the fence.
